 more  or less the same look from cars one in  the beginning of cars two with his  classic Rusty's logo on the back but in  the latest scene where he visits an old  disused Speedway track with Cruz Ramirez  we can see he's had a new paint job he's  now got a sort of souped up much larger  Rusty's logo on his side and another on  his back end he also has Lightning  McQueen emblazoned in bright fluorescent  letters just above his side windows and  later in a pit stop seen the Rusty's  logo has changed again reducing back  down in size but still different to the  style from the first two movies  Jackson's storm is clearly  new champion on the block and we can see  him collecting an award presumably the  Piston Cup and all the wild lightning is  looking on from the corner his number  looks like 20 but the design has  inserted a small point between the 2 and  the 0 which feels like a subtle  reference to the fact that storm  represents the upcoming new generation  of racecars so he's kind of version 2.0  and also the symbol on the side of  Jackson storm is appropriately enough  based on the international hurricane  symbol it's been tweaked and stretched  and color matched with his other blue  colors to give him a sleek look the  trailer also flashes through some of the  tech that is powering the new upstart  racer the screen show how he can change  his tire pressure  according to track conditions and also  which race trackies on and he's also  perfected his skills and speed with  access to a racing simulator there's a  neat by-and-large  Easter Egg which you can spot as a track  sponsor at one of the speed waves and  this could be a further clue that ties  the cars franchise into John new grones  Pixar theory remember BNL as the  corporation in Wally basically enabled a  pollution of the planet and sent humans  away from Earth while it attempted to  clear it up the Pixar theory suggests  that cars takes place after humans leave  the planet and before a time hundreds of  